# DTF tier manifest: conda-attestation-trust  (artifact-keeper#4556, #4155,
# #4058, #4709, #4711)
# Profile-set: filesystem / single. Entirely local: the signing key is a P-256
# key pair the oracle generates at run time (openssl), so no Fulcio, no Rekor
# and no network are involved, and no key material is committed.
#
# THE FEATURES / FIXES
# #4556 (1.11.0)  operator CEP-27 trust policy. CONDA_ATTESTATION_PUBLIC_KEYS
#        trusts public keys for key-based bundles (`cosign attest-blob --key`);
#        GET /api/v1/attestations/policy reports the policy (fingerprints, never
#        key bytes); a verified record says `method: sigstore-key` and the key
#        fingerprint; CEP-50 sidecars `<file>.sigs` / `.sigs.<sha256>` serve
#        the stored bundles (append-only, identical bundle not duplicated) and
#        every repodata record advertises `attestations_sha256`; a verified
#        attestation satisfies `predicates.conda.min_attestation_state` on the
#        download gate and `require_signature` on promotion, whose response
#        lists passed `gate_results`.
# #4155 (1.11.0)  attestations are verified, fail closed; the
#        CONDA_ATTESTATION_REQUIRE_VERIFIED=false opt-out stores the failed
#        record instead of refusing.
# #4058 (1.11.0)  scan-policy `predicates.conda` are enforced on download.
# #4709 / #4711 (1.11.2)  ATTESTATION_VERIFIED audit rows and the
#        ak_conda_attestation_total{outcome="verified"|"failed"} counters.
#
# The oracle recreates the backend twice with fixtures/attestation-keys.yml
# (first with the generated key trusted, then also with the opt-out), so the
# manifest's profile set is only the starting stack.
#
# RED: ak-backend:1.10.0 for every 1.11.0 case (no policy route, key bundles
# refused by the old shape check, predicates ignored, no sidecars);
# ak-backend:1.11.1 for the 1.11.2 audit/metric cases only.
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: one admin login then ~40 authenticated calls.
PROFILES="storage.filesystem"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
